WEBVTT

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:46.321
It may not be what you are
used to, but it is defensible.

00:00:46.404 --> 00:00:49.282
Peter. You may want to see this.

00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:06.800
It's us.

00:01:09.177 --> 00:01:11.221
What is this place?

00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:14.265
You don't know?

00:02:51.154 --> 00:02:53.072
He must know what he's doing.

00:03:00.163 --> 00:03:02.123
I think it's up to us now.

00:03:35.365 --> 00:03:37.575
(Peter) It's only a matter of time.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:41.579
Miraz's men and war machines
are on their way.

00:03:41.663 --> 00:03:45.458
That means those same men
aren't protecting his castle.

00:03:45.541 --> 00:03:47.293
What do you propose we do,
Your Majesty?

00:03:47.377 --> 00:03:50.004
- We need to get ready for it.
- To start planning for...

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:58.304
Our only hope is to strike them
before they strike us.

00:03:58.388 --> 00:04:00.181
Crazy. No one
has taken that castle.

00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:03.810
- There's always a first time.
- We'll have the element of surprise.

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:06.771
- But we have the advantage here!
- If we dig in,

00:04:06.854 --> 00:04:09.732
we could probably hold
them off indefinitely.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.487
(Trufflehunter) I, for one,
feel safer underground.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.657
Look. I appreciate
what you've done here,

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.326
but this isn't a fortress.
It's a tomb.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.328
Yes. And if they're smart,

00:04:22.412 --> 00:04:24.872
the Telmarines
will just wait and starve us out.

00:04:24.956 --> 00:04:28.835
- We could collect nuts!
- Yes! And throw them at the Telmarines.

00:04:28.918 --> 00:04:31.004
Shut up!

00:04:31.087 --> 00:04:33.089
I think you know where I stand, sire.

00:04:37.802 --> 00:04:41.764
If I get your troops in,
can you handle the guards?

00:04:46.102 --> 00:04:49.314
Or die trying, my liege.

00:04:49.397 --> 00:04:51.107
(Lucy) That's what I'm worried about.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.028
Sorry?

00:04:55.111 --> 00:04:58.031
You're all acting like
there's only two options.

00:04:58.114 --> 00:05:00.616
Dying here, or dying there.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.495
- I'm not sure you've been listening.
- No, you're not listening.

00:05:04.579 --> 00:05:07.832
Or have you forgotten who really
defeated the White Witch, Peter?

00:05:10.293 --> 00:05:13.129
I think we've waited
for Aslan long enough.

